@startuml seq-agentic-flow
title Mercury - Sequenza: flusso agentico (issue -> branch -> agent -> PR -> merge -> doc)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"

actor "Umano\n(architetto)" as H
participant "GitHub Issues" as GH
participant "Agent CLI\n(Claude Code /\nCodex CLI)" as AG
participant "Repository\nlocale + branch" as REPO
participant "PR su GitHub" as PR
participant "GitHub Actions\n(CI)" as CI
participant "docs/" as DOC

H -> GH: apre issue (specifica)\nrequisiti, scope, vincoli
H -> AG: prompt iniziale +\nriferimento issue #N
activate AG
AG -> REPO: crea branch\ncodex/issue-N-<slug>
AG -> DOC: legge guidelines\n(AGENTS, CLAUDE.md,\nCODEX.md, docs/*)
AG -> REPO: implementa modifiche\n(codice + log + test +\nlocalizzazione + docs)
AG -> REPO: commit(s) atomici
AG -> PR: apre PR (template completo)
deactivate AG

PR -> CI: trigger workflow
activate CI
CI -> CI: build iOS
CI -> CI: unit tests
CI -> CI: docs sync check
CI -> CI: markdown lint
CI -> CI: localization check
CI --> PR: status checks
deactivate CI

alt CI verde
  H -> PR: review umana\n(architettura, intent)
  alt approvato
    H -> PR: merge
    PR -> REPO: merge su main
    H -> DOC: (eventuale) refine doc\npost-merge
  else richiesta modifica
    H -> AG: feedback / nuovo prompt
    AG -> REPO: nuovi commit sulla stessa branch
    REPO -> PR: aggiorna PR
  end
else CI rossa
  AG -> REPO: fix + nuovo commit
  REPO -> PR: ri-trigger CI
end

note over H, DOC
  Governance: i documenti
  in docs/guidelines/ sono
  il "system prompt" implicito
  che vincola ogni agente.
end note

@enduml
